    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d470">

                <pb facs="0750" n="648" sameAs="frus:frus1933v01/pg648"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">550.S1/993: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the American Delegation</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hull</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-06-18T20:00:00+01:00">June 18, 1933—8
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 18—5:52 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>42. For your information, press reports that American delegation has proposed 10
                    percent all around tariff cut. We have made no such proposal but have merely
                    listed various topics<anchor n="59" xml:id="d470-f1"/> on the economic agenda
                    for discussion, which does not in the least constitute a statement of our
                    position.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d470-f1" n="59" xml:id="d470-f1-content">
                <p>Entitled: “Suggested Agenda for Economic Commission in the field of tariffs and
                    commercial policy” (Conf. M. B./C. E. 4.).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
